# What earns a line here, now that this folder is its own repository rather than a directory of
# the monorepo it came out of. The monorepo's .gitignore used to cover all of it; a clone of this
# repository has none of that.

# Claude Code session settings and worktrees. A session creates its worktree in whatever folder
# it is working in, and a worktree is a full copy of the repository. The machine's global ignore
# file covers .claude/settings.local.json already; that is a property of this machine, not of
# this repository, so it is written down here as well.
.claude/

# Build intermediates. Source/Directory.Build.props sends them here, OUTSIDE Mod/, and that
# placement is not a matter of taste: SteamUGC.SetItemContent uploads the published folder as it
# stands on disk with no filtering, so an obj/ inside Mod/ would publish the publicised
# Assembly-CSharp.dll - the game's own code - to every subscriber.
.build/

# Art/ is NOT ignored. The uncropped showcase sources and the two oversized original textures are
# tracked on purpose: ATTRIBUTION.md points at Art/textures-original/ as the record of what the
# rescaled textures were cut from, and a link to a file nobody has is worth nothing.

# Compressed copies the game writes next to the PNGs it loads: 80 of them here, 21 MB, first written
# on 2026-09-23 at 14:12, eighteen minutes before the Workshop item was created. Never a source (the
# PNG is), regenerated by the game whenever it wants, and never committed. Ignored so that a
# `git add -A` cannot take them, and so that a CI publish, which builds from a checkout, does not
# ship what an upload of the working folder did.
*.dds

# Test evidence. Pickle reports, captures and films stay on disk and never enter git: a capture is
# about 3 MB, a run leaves a dozen, and the runner's Player.log carries a personal path. The
# runner writes the folder with a capital E, so both spellings, at any depth. What is kept, and how
# small, is in docs/runs/README.md; the repository holds that text and nothing else.
evidence/
Evidence/
*.webm
